    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by the elite 80.22 score assigned to **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who faces Liberatore in a high-leverage spot that leverages his strong platoon advantage and prime #2 order placement. Following closely is the UTIL slot\u2019s **Cole Carrigg**, whose score of 71.23 is bolstered by a favorable 4.55 xERA matchup against Lugo and a significant +14% park factor, making him a high-efficiency engine for the day. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces an elite arm in Wheeler, his 68.30 score remains robust; he is effectively weaponized by an elite park factor and aggressive order placement, though we are monitoring his efficiency against Wheeler\u2019s ability to suppress the stolen base.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's docket was omitting **Luis Lara** from the starting OF rotation. Despite his respectable 50.28 score and the favorable 4.51 xERA offered by Ure\u00f1a, he narrowly missed the cut due to the superior base projections and higher-upside platoon splits of our locked-in OF trio. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** (64.28) and **Jackson Merrill** (63.41) provide the necessary speed and contact profiles to exploit their respective matchups, justifying their starts over the high-floor but lower-ceiling bench options like **Miguel Vargas**. We are exercising caution with **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** as their lineup spots are currently pending; should those official orders shift lower than projected, we may see a fluctuation in their current 63.49 and 62.57 scores. \n\nFinally, managers should keep a sharp eye on the 59.93 rating for **Liam Hicks**. While his matchup against Stock\u2019s 9.14 xERA is the most favorable pitching environment on the board, he remains a volatile play; his success is heavily tied to maintaining his high-volume recency trend. We have successfully avoided the bottom-tier production of **Wade Meckler** and **Denzer Guzman**, both of whom fell below our 40.0 floor due to Misiorowski\u2019s daunting 2.07 xERA. We remain fully committed to aggressive base-running profiles, with **Cole Carrigg** and **Gunnar Henderson** serving as our primary conduits for maintaining our edge in the scarce stolen base category.",
